# Env / secrets
#
# Real environment files hold live credentials -- the Clerk secret key, the Neon
# password, R2 access keys, the Confluent API secret. None of them belong in a
# repository, and this one is public.
#
# `.env.*` rather than a list of names. The variants multiply -- .env.production,
# .env.staging, .env.development, .env.production.local, and whatever the next
# tool decides to read -- and a list only protects the ones somebody thought of
# in advance. Ignore the shape instead, then carve the templates back out.
#
# No leading slash on any of these, so they match at every depth: frontend/.env
# is covered by the same rule as the root one.
.env
.env.*

# ...except templates, which carry key NAMES and no values, and are the only
# documentation of what a deployment actually needs.
#
# Order is load-bearing. Git applies the last matching pattern, so these
# negations have to follow the `.env.*` above -- moved before it, they do
# nothing and the templates silently vanish from the repository.
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

*.local

# Node / Next.js
node_modules/
.next/
out/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Java / Gradle / Maven
backend-spring/target/
backend-spring/build/
backend-spring/.gradle/
*.class

# Python
ai-service/.venv/
ai-service/venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# IDE / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Data
pgdata/
miniodata/
*.log

# Benchmark media and ground-truth transcripts.
#
# Never committed. The audio is third-party material we do not own, and the
# reference transcripts are derived from it. Developers drop their own files
# here locally; see docs/transcription-benchmark.md.
benchmark-audio/*
!benchmark-audio/README.md


